": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise \"FIN-212\", so I couldn't check it directly. The fix follows the test and the existing docstring instead. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}